sva.tooltip.garage.summary=§7Repairs the vehicle on its floor, installs tuning
sva.tooltip.garage.details=The floor is "Garage Lift Pads" laid next to the garage on its level (like charging platform plates; the size decides which vehicle fits). The screen: the vehicle's condition (hull and wear, engine heat, charge, drill head), repair "Repair all" (hull and engine cool-down) or "Hull only": %s EU per hull point and up to %s steel ingots for a whole hull (%s iron ingots instead of a steel one), 4 tuning slots. Silicon Age or IC2 network, HV input, %s EU buffer.
sva.tooltip.howto.garage=Place the garage with lift pads round it, drive in, right-click the garage. Metal goes in the screen's two slots. In the garage the vehicle's owner and players he gave the "Repair" right may repair (anyone may patch the hull by right-clicking the vehicle with a steel ingot); only the owner installs tuning. A comparator reads the repair's progress. Made on the Engineering Workbench.
sva.tooltip.garagePlate.summary=§7Floor of a "Repair Garage"
sva.tooltip.garagePlate.lamp=§eWork lamp - glows (light 12)
sva.tooltip.garagePlate.details=Plates touching each other and the garage on its level make a floor of any shape (up to %s plates). The floor's size decides which vehicle fits: 3x3 - hoverbike and buggy, 3x5 - crawler and drill vehicle, 5x5 - helicopter, plane and tiltrotor, 7x7 - jet, shuttle and Singular Ship.
sva.tooltip.howto.garagePlate=Lay the plates level with the garage, starting next to it. Made on the Engineering Workbench.
sva.tooltip.tuning.motor1=§7+15%% top speed
sva.tooltip.tuning.motor1.details=15%% faster. EU use and heat at full speed grow by themselves (they depend on speed). One motor only: I or II.
sva.tooltip.tuning.motor2=§7+30%% top speed
sva.tooltip.tuning.motor2.details=30%% faster. EU use and heat at full speed grow by themselves. Not together with "Motor+ I". Made from "Motor+ I".
sva.tooltip.tuning.battery=§7+50%% EU buffer
sva.tooltip.tuning.battery.details=The vehicle's buffer is half as big again. Take it out and the extra charge is lost. On the model: a box with a cyan stripe at the back.
sva.tooltip.tuning.armor=§7-40%% hull damage, -5%% speed
sva.tooltip.tuning.armor.details=Hits, crashes and hard landings wear the hull 40%% less. Wheeled, tracked vehicles and the hoverbike lose 5%% speed. Not together with "Light Hull". On the model: armour plates on the sides.
sva.tooltip.tuning.lightHull=§7+10%% speed, -20%% hull strength
sva.tooltip.tuning.lightHull.details=A lighter hull: 10%% faster but 20%% less maximum hull strength. Not together with "Armour".
sva.tooltip.tuning.bigWheels=§7Climbs 1.5 blocks
sva.tooltip.tuning.bigWheels.details=A wheeled vehicle drives up steps of up to 1.5 blocks without a jump. The wheels on the model are bigger.
sva.tooltip.tuning.lightBar=§7Headlight range x2
sva.tooltip.tuning.lightBar.details=Headlight beams twice as long, blocks ahead lit twice as far. A bar of four lamps on the roof.
sva.tooltip.tuning.drillPlus=§7Drill digs 1.5x faster
sva.tooltip.tuning.drillPlus.details=The drill head's dig speed x1.5 (the head still wears per block).
sva.tooltip.tuning.extraTank=§7+50%% gas in the tanks
sva.tooltip.tuning.extraTank.details=Every gas tank of an aircraft is half as big again. Take it out and the extra gas is lost. On the model: a belly tank.
sva.tooltip.tuning.fits=Fits: %s
sva.tooltip.tuning.fitsAll=any vehicle
sva.tooltip.howto.tuning=Installed only in a "Repair Garage": the vehicle on the garage floor, the upgrade into a tuning slot (up to %s). Only the owner installs and removes. Made on the Engineering Workbench ("Modules" tab).
sva.tooltip.tuningList=§7Tuning: §f%s
