# ---- aircraft stage A: flaps, slats, spoilers / airbrake (HighLiftMath)
sva.fn.flapsUp=Flaps -
sva.fn.flapsUp.tip=Retract the flaps a step: light plane 35 - 20 - 10 - 0 deg, jet 40 - 20 - 0. A step takes 1.5 s; they retract at any speed.
sva.fn.flapsUp.tilt=Flaperons -
sva.fn.flapsUp.tilt.tip=Retract the flaperons a step: 25 - 15 - 0 deg. They work in airplane mode; in vertical mode they droop by themselves.
sva.fn.flapsDown=Flaps +
sva.fn.flapsDown.tip=Extend the flaps a step: a lower stall speed and a shorter take-off run, but more drag and EU. A setting doesn't extend over its speed (35 deg - 120 km/h); too fast, the flaps go back a step by themselves. The slats work by themselves (AUTO): at a low speed and always with the flaps down.
sva.fn.flapsDown.tilt=Flaperons +
sva.fn.flapsDown.tilt.tip=Extend the flaperons a step (0 - 15 - 25 deg): an airplane take-off run up to a third shorter. Not over 140 and 120 km/h. In a bank they work as ailerons too.
sva.fn.airbrake=Airbrake
sva.fn.airbrake.tip=In the air - the spoilers (the jet: the speed brake behind the canopy): a steep descent without speeding up. Retracts by itself over half throttle. On the ground the spoilers come up by themselves at a touch-down at low throttle - the wheel brakes grip, a shorter roll-out.
