tile.siliconagevehicles.papi.name=PAPI Lights
tile.siliconagevehicles.approachLight.name=Approach Lights
sva.tooltip.papi.summary=§7Glide slope: white above, red below - 2 + 2 = on the slope
sva.tooltip.papi.details=One block is one unit with two lenses. Put 4 in a row by the runway edge, opposite the touchdown point: the heading comes from the runway itself, a unit's place in the row from how many units stand between it and the runway. A unit is white seen from above its angle and red from below: 3.5 / 3.2 / 2.8 / 2.5 deg from the one nearest the runway (3 deg nominal). RMB sets the whole row to 3 / 4 / 5 deg. Seen only from the approach; at night and in rain with a halo. A redstone part next to it (lever, wire...) switches it on / off by hand. The autopilot's CAP flies by them: RWY - G/S - FLARE.
sva.tooltip.howto.papi=Engineering Workbench: steel ingot x2, glass x2, glowstone, controller, red dye, iron x2 -> x4.
sva.tooltip.approachLight.summary=§7A pole with a lamp bar before the threshold, a running flash toward the runway
sva.tooltip.approachLight.details=Put them in a line on the runway's centre line before the threshold, every 2-4 blocks (up to 64 blocks out). The bar turns across the runway; poles stack. At night and in rain the lamps burn and a flash runs to the threshold twice a second. A redstone part next to it (lever, wire...) switches it on / off by hand.
sva.tooltip.howto.approachLight=Crafting table: glowstone dust x2, glass pane, iron x3, redstone -> x2.
