sva.tooltip.bat.services=§7Serviced %s times (limit %s%%)
sva.tooltip.bat.details=Fits only the "%s" - the slot takes no other vehicle's battery. Charges in the core's energy storages of tier %s and up (and in IC2), in the vehicle from the generator while the engine runs and at a vehicle charging station. Without a battery the engine can't start and the lights, instruments and autopilot are dead.
sva.tooltip.howto.bat=Install: right-click the vehicle with it or put it into the "Battery" slot (cargo screen, "Vehicle" tab). Remove: there, or "Remove" in the "Vehicle" menu - only with the engine off, by the owner or a player with the "Repair" right. A spare can ride in the cargo. Wear: charge cycles and deep discharges; service it in the repair garage or with the service kit.
sva.tooltip.electrolyte=§7Consumable for servicing vehicle batteries
sva.tooltip.electrolyte.details=One item is one service: the repair garage's "Service battery" (%s EU) or the battery service kit in the field.
sva.tooltip.howto.electrolyte=Garage: put it into the metal slots. Kit: keep it in your inventory. Recipe: water bottle, core NaOH bucket, redstone.
sva.tooltip.batteryKit=§7Right-click a vehicle: +%s%% battery health
sva.tooltip.batteryKit.details=Uses 1 electrolyte from the inventory, takes %s s; the engine off, stay close. Not over the limit, and the limit drops %s%% as in the garage.
sva.tooltip.howto.batteryKit=Right-click your vehicle with the kit (or one you have the "Repair" right for). The kit is not used up.
sva.tooltip.jumpCables=§7Jump start: up to %s%% of the battery in %s s
sva.tooltip.jumpCables.donor=§aConnected to a donor - now right-click your vehicle
sva.tooltip.jumpCables.details=The donor gives charge while it keeps at least %s%%; the vehicles within %s blocks of each other.
sva.tooltip.howto.jumpCables=Right-click the donor vehicle with the cables, then your own. A charged core battery right-clicked on a vehicle also pours its charge into the vehicle battery.
