sva.tooltip.tuning.ramCoat=§7Radars see the vehicle 40%% closer
sva.tooltip.tuning.ramCoat.details=Air-defence radars detect the vehicle at x0.6 of their range (with "Smooth Hull" x0.54). Aircraft only.
sva.tooltip.tuning.smoothHull=§7Radars see the vehicle 10%% closer
sva.tooltip.tuning.smoothHull.details=Air-defence radars detect the vehicle at x0.9 of their range. Not together with "Armour". Aircraft only.
sva.tooltip.tuning.rwr=§7Radar warning in the cockpit
sva.tooltip.tuning.rwr.details=Who paints the vehicle and from where: surveillance (S), height finder (H), a tracking lock (T), a missile (M) - on the cockpit's RWR scope, in the HUD (third person) and by sound: a soft beep, a loud tone, a siren. Aircraft only.
sva.tooltip.radar.summary=§7Range §f%s blocks§7 (a light plane: %s), §f%s EU/t§7 (%s)
sva.tooltip.radar.survey.details=The antenna turns once in 6 s: it sees every flying vehicle in the circle (place +-8 blocks, no altitude) and reads the transponders (code, altitude in mode C, board in mode S). The range grows with the vehicle's RCS (ship 600, light plane 337, jet 313), rain -15%%, a storm -30%%. Stone, earth and metal between the antenna and the target hide it, leaves and glass do not. Ground vehicles are not seen.
sva.tooltip.radar.track.details=Holds two targets at once, twice a second: the exact place and altitude. The missile system needs it to launch; the command post picks the targets (assigned, violators, strangers). A pilot with a radar warning receiver sees the lock.
sva.tooltip.radar.height.details=Every 3 s gives the altitude of every target in range - silent transponders too. Without the altitude zones with a height band do not work.
sva.tooltip.howto.radar=Place within 64 blocks of your command post and power it. Higher up - less terrain shadow. RMB: the radar's screen (the scope, the state, the modules). Made on the Engineering Workbench ("Blocks" tab).
sva.tooltip.launcher.gun=§7A gun up to §f%s blocks§7, §f%s EU/t§7 (MV)
sva.tooltip.launcher.gun.details=Twin barrels: a burst of 3 shells every 0.5 s, 10 hull points a hit. Fires on the command post's data (on the surveillance radar - with a spread) or by its own eyes up to 48 blocks. Ammunition: "AA Shells" (one item - one burst).
sva.tooltip.launcher.missile=§7Missiles up to §f%s blocks§7, §f%s EU/t§7 (EV)
sva.tooltip.launcher.missile.details=4 tubes, two fire channels (two missiles in the air). Launches only at a target a tracking radar holds (or within 48 blocks). The missile: 3 blocks a tick, 8 s, a 3-block proximity fuse, 110 hull points; behind the terrain it loses the target. A launch costs 20 000 EU.
sva.tooltip.howto.launcher=Place within 64 blocks of your command post and power it. RMB - its screen: rules of engagement, warnings, radius, ammunition; Shift+RMB with ammunition - load it. No fire while the server is in the "warnings only" mode. Engineering Workbench.
sva.tooltip.kp.summary=§7Links radars and launchers within §f%s blocks§7, §f%s EU/t§7 (MV)
sva.tooltip.kp.details=One picture of all your radars: tracks, data blocks, airspace zones, the log. Target assignment, "friendly for 10 min", the alarm (redstone 15 on every side), a message to the pilot. The day key's secret, own codes, the Mode S white list.
sva.tooltip.howto.kp=RMB - the command post's screen (the owner and his access list). RMB with a "Code Card" - prints the day's code on it. Engineering Workbench. The "Equipment" tab: energy and modules.
sva.tooltip.ammo.aaShells=§7A burst: §f%s§7 shells, up to §f%s blocks
sva.tooltip.ammo.aaShells.details=For the AA gun: one item - one burst, %s hull points a hit.
sva.tooltip.ammo.samMissile=§7Range §f%s blocks§7, damage §f%s
sva.tooltip.ammo.samMissile.details=For the missile system: one missile a tube. Homing, a 3-block proximity fuse.
sva.tooltip.howto.ammo=Into the launcher's slots (its screen) or Shift+RMB on it. Crafting table: shells - iron, gunpowder, steel; the missile - a sensor, a controller, steel casings, gunpowder, blaze powder.
sva.tooltip.codeCard.blank=§7Blank: print a code at a command post
